From: naelolaiz <1333555+naelolaiz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: esp32s31: softmac: scan and join channels 12 and 13

The softmac frontend registers 2.4 GHz channels 1 to 11 only and drops
received frames from any other channel. The radio firmware already sets
an ESP-IDF country with channels 1 to 13 (s31_wifi_prepare() in
firmware/radio/radio_stack.c) and accepts S31_WIFI_SET_CHANNEL up to 13,
so only the Linux side keeps the station off channels 12 and 13.

Routers in Europe pick those channels too. With the router on channel
13 (2472 MHz) the board saw 38 other networks and kept scanning for its
own one.

Register 13 channels and accept received frames from all of them.
cfg80211 still decides where the station may transmit: with the world
regulatory domain, channels 12 and 13 start as no-IR (passive scan only)
until a beacon is seen there.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/espressif/esp32s31_softmac.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/espressif/esp32s31_softmac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/espressif/esp32s31_softmac.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/espressif/esp32s31_softmac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/espressif/esp32s31_softmac.c
@@ -179,7 +179,8 @@
 	bool tx_ba_requested, tx_ba_operational, tx_native_peer, tx_ba_flushing;
 	u32 tx_ampdu_submitted;
 	u8 channel;
-	struct ieee80211_channel channels[11];
+	/* 2.4 GHz channels 1 to 13; the radio firmware sets a 1-13 country. */
+	struct ieee80211_channel channels[13];
 	struct ieee80211_rate rates[12];
 	struct ieee80211_supported_band band;
 	struct ieee80211_sband_iftype_data iftype;
@@ -929,7 +930,7 @@
 		   length >= sizeof(struct s31_softmac_rx_header) + 24 &&
 		   length <= sizeof(struct s31_softmac_rx_header) + S31_SOFTMAC_FRAME_MAX &&
 		   meta.encoding <= 2 && meta.rate_index < (meta.encoding == 1 ? 8 : meta.encoding == 2 ? 10 : ARRAY_SIZE(sm->rates)) &&
-		   channel >= 1 && channel <= 11) {
+		   channel >= 1 && channel <= ARRAY_SIZE(sm->channels)) {
 		u8 rate = meta.rate_index;
 		u8 encoding = meta.encoding, phy_flags = meta.flags;
 
-- 
